*Standing.* Multiple reviewers presented published neutronics results showing solid‑Be multipliers achieve net TBR ≈1.5, whereas Pb‑based designs are limited to ≈1.3. These contradictions directly falsify the claim that the Pb configuration provides the highest achievable net TBR.
